      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm studying for my con law exam and im a bit stuck on judicial philosophy. can u explain what the main arguments are for originalism in constitutional interpretation? like, what are the actual legal justifications for it?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Originalism argues that the Constitution should be interpreted according to the meaning it had at the time it was ratified. Proponents justify this by emphasizing that the text is the supreme law, and judges should not impose their own subjective policy preferences onto it. This approach grounds its authority in the democratic principle that the people, through their elected representatives, established the original meaning. Therefore, originalism seeks to constrain judicial power to the historical intent of the framers.",
